/inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKANO SHINJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIOKA YOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADA YUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKASE HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YABUHARA TADAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAMESHIMA, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKANO, SHINJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIOKA, YOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, YUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKASE, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YABUHARA, TADAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A powdery flame retardant which is obtained by mixing a flame retardant which is liquid or a viscous solid at ordinary temperature with an inorganic fibrous substance to adhere or adsorb the retardant to the fibrous substance, and which comprises 5 to 70 wt.% the flame retardant and 95 to 30 wt.% the fibrous substance. The powdery flame retardant can be easily handled because it is a powder, and is obtained by a simple and industrially advantageous method. It produces a remarkable effect that the performance of the liquid or viscous flame retardant is not impaired.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un ignifuge poudreux obtenu par mélange d'un ignifuge liquide ou visqueux solide à une température ordinaire avec une substance fibreuse inorganique pour produire une adhérence de l'ignifuge à la substance fibreuse ou une adsorption sur la substance fibreuse, cet ignifuge comprenant 5 à 70 % en poids d'ignifuge et 95 à 30 % en poids de substance fibreuse. L'ignifuge poudreux peut être facilement manipulé parce qu'il est sous forme de poudre, et est obtenu grâce à un procédé simple et avantageux sur le plan industriel. Il est remarquable que les propriétés de l'ignifuge liquide ou visqueux ne s'altèrent pas.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>